{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01M1K487ZT99MT9B84G99P5EJ6","title":"Write extraction for rename/copy verbs lives in the mapper, not in policy strings","decision":"The bash capability mapper emits fs.write for the destination of rename/copy/link verbs and expands tilde destinations to the session home, so home-anchored deny rules see the same capability regardless of the verb or path spelling.","alternatives":[{"option":"proc.exec string patterns per verb in policy.d","why_rejected":"matches command TEXT, so any command merely mentioning the verb and the path (commit messages, memory episodes, PR bodies) is gated; measured false positives the same day"},{"option":"policy-level fs.write aliases for known targets only","why_rejected":"would leave every other protected path open to the same verbs"}],"scope":["crates/gommage-core/src/shell.rs","crates/gommage-stdlib/capabilities/bash.yaml","crates/gommage-cli/src/input.rs"],"commits":["f55ab43bba5b6993d59ea264a03c7a2c501b245d"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1788422135802}
